\begin{aligned}
& \mathrm{CO}(6+8=14)=\sigma 1 s^2, \stackrel{*}{\sigma} 1 s^2, \\
& \sigma 2 s^2, \stackrel{*}{\sigma} 2 s^2, \pi 2 p_x^2 \approx \pi 2 p_y^2, \sigma 2 p_z^2
\end{aligned}

(All the electrons are paired so it is diamagneitc.)

\begin{aligned}
& \mathrm{O}_2^{-}(8+8+1=17) \\
& =\sigma 1 s^2, \stackrel{*}{\sigma} 1 s^2, \sigma 2 s^2, \stackrel{*}{\sigma} 2 s^2, \sigma 2 p_z^2, \pi 2 p_x^2 \\
& \approx \pi 2 p_y^2, \stackrel{*}{\pi} 2 p_x^2 \approx \stackrel{*}{\pi} 2 p_y^1
\end{aligned}

It contains one unpaired electron so it is paramagnetic.

\begin{aligned}
